{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbbDgrRXe6UCaPS2EBJK", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Only with `--dry-run`.\n\nA stored hazard memory says that in staging, `EXPORT_BUCKET` points at the **production** bucket. A real run against staging could therefore write to prod. The memory says never to run `scripts/export.py` against staging without `--dry-run`.\n\nThe script supports that flag. In its current form it only prints `exporting staging to <bucket> (dry_run=True)` and doesn't write anything, so a dry run is safe. It also lets you confirm which bucket staging resolves to:\n\n```\npython scripts/export.py --env staging --dry-run\n```\n\nIf the printed bucket is the prod one, the memory is still accurate.\n\nTwo caveats:\n- The script doesn't actually use `--dry-run` to gate anything yet, because it has no export logic. When real export code gets added, make sure it honors the flag before anyone relies on this.\n- I haven't run the command myself, since it depends on your staging environment variables. Say so if you want me to run it.\n\nFor a real (non-dry) staging test, point `EXPORT_BUCKET` at a dedicated test bucket first, for example `EXPORT_BUCKET=ledgerline-exports-staging-test`. That bucket name is only an example, so I'd confirm it exists and is separate from prod before using it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 549, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21281, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 549}, "output_tokens": 418, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1bad6326-0016-44d7-ac6b-6201b40d2f28", "uuid": "8552d5da-cf00-4c06-9c0f-8a49e93feb32", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:2